@startuml plano-control-datos-hub-mesh
title Hub-Mesh: Planos de Control y Datos

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE

rectangle "Plano de Control" as PC #E3F2FD {
    node "Orchestrator\n:8000" as Orch
    node "Peer A\n(IP pública)" as PA
    node "Peer B\n(IP pública)" as PB
    node "Peer C\n(NAT simétrico)" as PC2
}

rectangle "Plano de Datos" as PD #E8F5E9 {
    node "HUB\nwg-HUB :51820" as HUB
    node "Peer A\nwg0" as WGA
    node "Peer B\nwg0" as WGB
    node "Peer C\nwg0" as WGC
}

' Control plane
PA -up-> Orch : register/heartbeat\n+ nat_type
PB -up-> Orch : register/heartbeat\n+ nat_type
PC2 -up-> Orch : register/heartbeat\n+ nat_type

' Data plane - hybrid
WGA <-right-> WGB : WireGuard directo\n(ambos alcanzables)
WGA <-down-> HUB : WireGuard relay
WGB <-down-> HUB : WireGuard relay
WGC <-down-> HUB : WireGuard relay

note right of WGA
  **Data Flow - Directo**
  Peer A ↔ Peer B
  Ambos con IP pública
  1 salto, baja latencia
end note

note bottom of HUB
  **Data Flow - Relay**
  Peer C (NAT simétrico)
  Tráfico via HUB como fallback
  2 saltos, latencia media
end note

note bottom of Orch
  **Control Flow**
  - Clasifica peers:
    * direct (alcanzables)
    * relay_only (NAT simétrico)
  - probe_direct_peers()
  - peer.report_reachability()
end note

note bottom of PC2
  **Detección NAT**
  Orchestrator detecta nat_type
  y clasifica automáticamente:
  - none / full-cone → direct
  - symmetric → relay_only
end note

@enduml
